#. Tag: author
#: blackbody.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid "<firstname>Jasem</firstname> <surname>Mutlaq</surname>"
msgstr "<firstname>Jasem</firstname> <surname>Mutlaq</surname>"

#. Tag: title
#: blackbody.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Blackbody Radiation</title>"
msgstr "<title>Zračenje crnog tijela</title>"

#. Tag: primary
#: blackbody.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "<primary>Blackbody Radiation</primary>"
msgstr "<primary>Zračenje crnog tijela</primary>"

#. Tag: seealso
#: blackbody.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "Star Colors and Temperatures"
msgstr "Boje zvijezda i temperature"

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <firstterm>blackbody</firstterm> refers to an opaque object that emits "
"<firstterm>thermal radiation</firstterm>. A perfect blackbody is one that "
"absorbs all incoming light and does not reflect any. At room temperature, "
"such an object would appear to be perfectly black (hence the term "
"<emphasis>blackbody</emphasis>). However, if heated to a high temperature, a "
"blackbody will begin to glow with <firstterm>thermal radiation</firstterm>."
msgstr ""
"<firstterm>Crno tijelo</firstterm> odnosi se na neprozirne objekte koji "
"emituju <firstterm>toplotno zračenje</firstterm>. Savršeno crno tijelo je "
"ono koje apsorbuje svu dolazeću svjetlos i ne reflektuje nijednu. Na sobnoj "
"temperaturi, takav objekat će biti potpuno crn (otuda izraz <emphasis>crno "
"tijelo</emphasis>). Međutim, ako zagrijavate na visoke temperature, crno "
"tijelo će početi da isijava <firstterm>toplotno zračenje</firstterm>."

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In fact, all objects emit thermal radiation (as long as their temperature is "
"above Absolute Zero, or -273.15 degrees Celsius), but no object emits "
"thermal radiation perfectly; rather, they are better at emitting/absorbing "
"some wavelengths of light than others. These uneven efficiencies make it "
"difficult to study the interaction of light, heat and matter using normal "
"objects."
msgstr ""
"U stvari, svi objekti emitiraju toplotnog zračenja (dok je njihova "
"temperatura iznad apsolutne nule, ili -273,15 stupnjeva celzijusa), ali ne "
"postoji objekat koji emituje savršeno toplotno zračenje; umjesto toga, oni "
"su bolji u emitovanju/apsorpciji nekih talasnih dužina svjetlosti od drugih. "
"Ove nejednake efikasnosti otežavaju proučavanje interakcije svjetlosti, "
"toplote i materije koristeći normalne objekte."

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Fortunately, it is possible to construct a nearly-perfect blackbody. "
"Construct a box made of a thermally conductive material, such as metal. The "
"box should be completely closed on all sides, so that the inside forms a "
"cavity that does not receive light from the surroundings. Then, make a small "
"hole somewhere on the box. The light coming out of this hole will almost "
"perfectly resemble the light from an ideal blackbody, for the temperature of "
"the air inside the box."
msgstr ""
"Srećom, moguće je da se izgradi gotovo savršeno crno tijelo. Izraditi "
"kutijicu od toplinskih provodnih materijala, kao što su metal. Kutija treba "
"da bude potpuno zatvorena sa svih strana, tako da se formira unutra šupljina "
"koja ne prima svjetlo iz okoline. Zatim, napravite malu rupu negdje na "
"kutiji. Svjetlo koje dolazi iz ove rupe će gotovo savršeno liči svjetlu "
"idealnog crnog tijela, za temperaturu zraka unutar kutije."

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the beginning of the 20th century, scientists Lord Rayleigh, and Max "
"Planck (among others) studied the blackbody radiation using such a device. "
"After much work, Planck was able to empirically describe the intensity of "
"light emitted by a blackbody as a function of wavelength. Furthermore, he "
"was able to describe how this spectrum would change as the temperature "
"changed. Planck's work on blackbody radiation is one of the areas of physics "
"that led to the foundation of the wonderful science of Quantum Mechanics, "
"but that is unfortunately beyond the scope of this article."
msgstr ""
"Početkom 20. stoljeća, naučnici Lord Rayleigh, i Max Planck (između ostalih) "
"proučavali su radijaciju crnog tijela pomoću takvog uređaja. Nakon mnogo "
"rada, Planck je bio u mogućnosti da empirijski opiše intenzitet svjetlosti "
"koje emituje crno tijelo kao funkciju talasne dužine. Osim toga, on je bio u "
"mogućnosti da opiše kako bi se spektar mijenjao kako se temperatura mijenja. "
"Planckov rad na baziran na zračenju crnog tijela je jedna od oblasti fizike "
"koja je dovela do osnivanja divne nauke kvantne mehanike, ali to je, "
"nažalost, izvan opsega ovog članka."

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What Planck and the others found was that as the temperature of a blackbody "
"increases, the total amount of light emitted per second increases, and the "
"wavelength of the spectrum's peak shifts to bluer colors (see Figure 1)."
msgstr ""
"Što su Planck i ostali našli je da kada se temperatura crnog tijela "
"povećava, ukupan iznos svjetlosti emitovane u sekundi se povećava, a talasna "
"dužina vrha spektra se mijenja u nijanse plave boje (vidi figuru 1)."

#. Tag: phrase
#: blackbody.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "Figure 1"
msgstr "Figura 1"

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example, an iron bar becomes orange-red when heated to high temperatures "
"and its color progressively shifts toward blue and white as it is heated "
"further."
msgstr ""
"Na primjer, željezna šipka postaje crveno-narandžasta kad se zagrijava na "
"visoke temperature i njegova boja se postepeno pomiče prema plavoj i bijeloj "
"boji jer se i dalje zagrijava."

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In 1893, German physicist Wilhelm Wien quantified the relationship between "
"blackbody temperature and the wavelength of the spectral peak with the "
"following equation:"
msgstr ""
"Godine 1893., njemački fizičar Wilhelm Wien kvantificirao je odnos između "
"temperature crnog tijela i talasne dužine spektralnog vrha sljedećom "
"jednadžbom:"

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"where T is the temperature in Kelvin. Wien's law (also known as Wien's "
"displacement law) states that the wavelength of maximum emission from a "
"blackbody is inversely proportional to its temperature. This makes sense; "
"shorter-wavelength (higher-frequency) light corresponds to higher-energy "
"photons, which you would expect from a higher-temperature object."
msgstr ""
"gdje je T temperatura u Kelvinima. Wienov zakon (poznat i kao Wien-ov zakon "
"pomaka) navodi da je talasna dužina maksimalne emisije iz crnog tijela "
"obrnuto proporcionalna njegovoj temperaturi. To ima smisla; kraćim talasnim "
"dužinama (višefrekventnim) svjetla odgovara više energije fotona, što možete "
"očekivati od objekata sa višom temperaturom."

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example, the sun has an average temperature of 5800 K, so its wavelength "
"of maximum emission is given by:"
msgstr ""
"Na primjer, Sunce ima prosječnu temperaturu od 5800 K, tako da je njegova "
"talasna dužine maksimalne emisije data:"

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This wavelengths falls in the green region of the visible light spectrum, "
"but the sun's continuum radiates photons both longer and shorter than lambda"
"(max) and the human eyes perceives the sun's color as yellow/white."
msgstr ""
"Ova talasna dužina pada u zeleno područje vidljivog spektra svetlosti, ali "
"sunce je kontinuum koji zrači fotone i duže i kraće talasne dužine od lambda "
"(max) i ljudsko oko percipira sunčeve boje kao žuto/bijelo."

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In 1879, Austrian physicist Stephan Josef Stefan showed that the luminosity, "
"L, of a black body is proportional to the 4th power of its temperature T."
msgstr ""
"U 1879. austrijski fizičar Stephan Josef Stefan je pokazao da je blistavost, "
"L, crnog tijela proporcionalna 4. moći njegove temperature T."

#. Tag: para
#: blackbody.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"where A is the surface area, alpha is a constant of proportionality, and T "
"is the temperature in Kelvin. That is, if we double the temperature (e.g. "
"1000 K to 2000 K) then the total energy radiated from a blackbody increase "
"by a factor of 2<superscript>4</superscript> or 16."
msgstr ""
"gdje A je površina, alfa je konstanta proporcionalnosti, a T je temperatura "
"u Kelvinima. To jest, ako udvostručimo temperaturu (npr 1000 K do 2000 K), a "
"zatim ukupnu energiju zračenja iz crnog tijela povećamo za faktor "
"2<superscript>4</superscript> ili 16."

